  "text": "Skip to content\nDONATE\nInstagram X-twitter Facebook-f Tiktok\nDONATE\nInstagram X-twitter Facebook-f Tiktok\nInstagram X-twitter Facebook-f Tiktok\n# Endorsements\nA message from Will: I’m incredibly proud to have the support from over 100 local and national leaders and organizations. These folks know me from my leadership on housing and environmental issues, my service on local boards and coalitions, and in some cases, all the way back to my youth growing up in East Lansing. I am rooted in community and I will always work diligently to reward your trust.\n## 200+ Endorsers Including:\nMichigan AFL-CIO\nUnited Auto Workers\nSocial Security Works\nInternational Brotherhood of Electrical Workers - Local 665\nSierra Club\nInternational Association of Machinist and Aerospace Workers Local 698\nCommunications Workers of America\nNational Nurses United\nNorthern Midwest Regional Council of Carpenters\nJohn Hayhoe - Former Delhi Township Supervisor (R)\nBernie Sanders - US Senator\nState Senator Sarah Anthony\nKara Hope - State Representative\nEmily Dievendorf - State Representative\nTrini Pehlivanoglu - Lansing City Council\nDr. Lavontè Heard - Lansing Board of Education\nGuillermo Lopez - President, Lansing Board of Education\nRyan Bushard - President, Village of Dansville\nAndy Levin - Fmr. US Rep. (MI-9)\nCollin Baker - Leslie City Council Member\nJason Peek - Eaton County Commissioner\nUS Rep. Delia Ramirez\nLisa Dilg - South Lyon City Council\nUS Rep. Maxwell Frost\nUS Rep. Jamie Raskin\nJohn Andrews - Clinton County Commissioner\nUS Rep Pramila Jayapal\nRyan Kost - Lansing City Council\nLynn Jondahl - Former State Representative\nLeague of Conversation Voters Action Fund\nCommon Defense\nIndivisible\nA New Policy PAC\nWorking Families Party\nSunrise Movement\nProgressive Change Campaign Committee\nTrack AIPAC\nCongressional Progressive Caucus\nSEIU 517M\nUnited Food and Commercial Workers Local 951\nPlanned Parenthood Action Fund\nReproductive Freedom for All\nDCCC Red to Blue List\nOffice & Professional Employees International Union Local 459\nUnited Food and Commercial Workers Local 876\nMichigan Education Association\n×\n### Donate to fund our grassroots campaign\n$27\n$50\n$250\nOther",
